    <!-- Cell grid filling the left pool (x -9..-2.5 m, y -2.25..2.25 m): 13 x 9 open-topped cells,
         0.5 x 0.5 x 2 m, standing on the pool floor (z = -4.895 m). Cells in odd columns AND odd rows are
         control cells (light yellow); all others are fuel cells (blue), so every control cell is the
         centre of a 3 x 3 cluster of fuel cells. Collision per cell: floor plus four walls, so the
         cells stay hollow. -->
